  "result": "Perfect! I've added credit note support for refund tracking:\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added:\n- CREDIT_TOO_HIGH: Credit note amount exceeds invoice total\n\n**src/credits.js** \u2014 Added:\n- **nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)** \u2014 Generates credit note numbers:\n  - CN-<year>-<counter> format\n  - Separate counter from invoices\n  - 4-digit zero-padded counter, resets yearly\n  - Ignores invoice numbers in existingNumbers\n\n- **createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)** \u2014 Creates credit notes:\n  - Accepts invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n  - amount must be positive integer in cents (AMOUNT_INVALID if not)\n  - date must be valid 'YYYY-MM-DD' (DATE_INVALID if not)\n  - Rejects if amount exceeds invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n  - Rejects draft invoices (NOT_ISSUED)\n  - Returns ok({ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date })\n\n**Key design:**\n- Credit notes have independent numbering from invoices\n- Can credit any issued/paid invoice (including partially paid)\n- Validates against invoice total including all discounts and VAT\n- Tracks reason for audit trail\n- Date field allows backdating credit notes if needed\n\nAdded 18 tests covering numbering, status validation, amount validation, date validation, and separate counter handling. All 190 tests pass.",
